hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27665","Haddathana Hashim, he said: Haddathana Layth, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me from Ubayd Sanuta Abu al-Walid, he said: I heard Khawlah bint Qays ibn Qahd, and she was under Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever earns it rightfully, it is blessed for him therein, and many a one who plunges as his soul wishes into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger shall have nothing on the Day of Resurrection except the Fire."
"27666","Haddathana [source text truncated in index; only the opening word preserved]."
"27667","Haddathana [source text truncated in index; only the opening word preserved]."
